Looking at this question: "total revenue by location" — location is not part of the order_item model, but orders has a location entity. Revenue (per the governed term) for gross order-level revenue is `orders.order_total`, and location grouping requires `entity:orders.location` with `dimension:locations.location_name` as display.

Per rule 8b, "Revenue" is governed by term:Revenue, which says gross revenue including tax uses order_total from orders mart. Since the breakdown is by location (an orders/location-level dimension), this is the order-grain revenue.

